  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_cf224400a5134a65804f9480f7e6bb41",
      "statement": "GPT-OSS-Lite places a MoE layer in every transformer block; each layer flattens `(B, T, D)` input to tokens, routes them, adds routed and shared expert outputs, restores the original shape, and returns a scalar auxiliary loss. The model averages per-block auxiliary losses and returns that mean alongside vocabulary logits.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/moe.py#L64-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:744227fb09aa7ff7cec77482e78e920d84cbdce060ca05e670c4e4349d2bac3b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/transformer.py#L138-L153",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2ce8317e8fc28f7bc1cecd29be681d176bdb47c3bdff6e6c6721cb98a5bc1614:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/transformer.py#L186-L227",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:52783c07db9d7eb20febbe324704ed062617efbb773964f712954562f0292a20:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c8ff795faa194c78a16240e4b2422d83",
      "statement": "The default MoE topology is 8 routed experts with top-2 activation, 1 shared expert, `ffn_dim=1536`, and `moe_dispatch=\"stacked\"`; the default training configuration uses the same topology and sets `aux_loss_alpha: 0.01`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://configs/pretrain_a100_502m.yaml#L17-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dc94b93974339ee9a017f7183ecc04f86a6619bc807080f0a9abe613f948e352:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/transformer.py#L23-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:602b25249756c32e45017d253488313e8b0bea1850dced5e7cb9104527f2a4fa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_68f12f89a52c44c5af652cca6622aef3",
      "statement": "Each routed or shared expert is a bias-free SwiGLU module computing `W2(F.silu(W1(x)) * W3(x))`, with W1 and W3 projecting to the intermediate width and W2 projecting back to the model width.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/moe.py#L11-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e163591b8f1419d0c4c8548eb45aa087dc493206553554f7e3bf48ecbc3cc2a0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3703b52150f94e009d9c178045059cac",
      "statement": "The router is a bias-free linear gate that computes softmax over all routed experts in FP32, selects exactly `n_activated` top probabilities, renormalizes the selected probabilities with a `1e-6` minimum denominator, returns those weights in the input dtype, and retains raw logits for auxiliary-loss computation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/moe.py#L24-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:418fdcdd18bed1e21d78aa4b9cb60472381235768898643074125eb9a27b1e2f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_moe.py#L38-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:274b2b3813967550fdf69445f9cdb1c0585aaf63a6972378b5f75b503f9b87f2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_08ebdca829a643438f34930c555d08ed",
      "statement": "The auxiliary objective is the standard Switch/GShard-style `E * sum(f * P)`: `f` is the hard top-k slot frequency from `bincount`, `P` is the mean FP32 softmax probability, and only the final scalar is cast back to the logits dtype. The training loop adds this loss to cross-entropy with coefficient 0.01 before gradient-accumulation scaling.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://configs/pretrain_a100_502m.yaml#L64-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d0db58d011fff3b02ec6c511fab0c56433d400d6aa302294cb3e5262b50d3ab1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/moe.py#L46-L61",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c7c3fb0ab5b8ff7e23acf11542dfc76a8d8604bbdc3217fc001b26254e6f0000:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://training/pretrain.py#L350-L399",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cc747f28c36595bb4999fdc11cd87e41f5c10be5aafade12762fd6b99d618d4d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1daa25ce0353432a9a7defad25a79d13",
      "statement": "Shared experts bypass routing: when configured, each shared SwiGLU runs on every flattened token and its output is summed directly into the routed result without router weights.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/moe.py#L95-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:389186c3a0aba08c41a0e688e2fbcf1f1c313a03ae0c3aa6bd8bd3f28270983f:"
        },
        {
