    {
      "id": "claim_466a7f395056431b8a7deb33b77298f1",
      "statement": "The explicitly opt-in Triton path replaces only the routed W1/W3 plus SiLU and elementwise multiplication stage. `_dispatch_triton` keeps expert grouping, applies per-expert W2 in PyTorch, scales by routing weights, and scatters with the same accumulation contract; router computation, auxiliary loss, shared experts, and other model components remain outside the fused kernel.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/moe.py#L107-L166",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cc51d2ea13ef7ac242b56d8d7ed767cc29b6b6a6f5ae3815e8eb0f0a069cd7ba:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/moe_triton.py#L1-L5",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f89617fc1c928f643f008966d32585bb742dcc5695fafa2f32e4254e0f29a17e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/moe_triton.py#L205-L222",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cb578450cf9c5c592a7bc5f9602a53bf497b08e58e3e512885754e74c402a780:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_71e0c39abaa74d05be16f9ef5293a06e",
      "statement": "The Triton kernel uses a three-dimensional expert/token-tile/intermediate-tile launch with fixed `BLOCK_T=16`, `BLOCK_M=32`, and `BLOCK_N=32`; it masks partial token, feature, and reduction tiles, accumulates W1 and W3 products in FP32, disables TF32 for tiled dots, applies SiLU in FP32, and casts the fused result to the output dtype.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/moe_triton.py#L147-L181",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:006060d3fbd3f7a3d46d0dfcfefca9871fac7a552e8dd8b126a920e88b7613b6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/moe_triton.py#L53-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e668dd289319268842cc3e457ea3e3b21dfc95b16fc488bccd3601fc1128b16d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7505c4a9fa824be8b403d27c0df919a9",
      "statement": "The Triton operation is wrapped in a custom autograd Function whose forward launches the kernel and whose backward recomputes `_moe_w1w3_silu_reference` under `torch.enable_grad()` to obtain gradients for sorted inputs, W1, and W3; expert ids, counts, and offsets receive no gradients.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/concepts/kernels-and-checkpointing.md#L158-L183",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:80b0a65578a9299ce617618f420fa370268a9a1b3da3376cc894d4496e5b2634:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/moe_triton.py#L135-L202",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:df4d4f17d4f69cfa1c141c2c468a378d5ce36c0a4cb0425eeddb568caa0732b4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_933f086a2606428c87b20c257b4a7f21",
      "statement": "Triton availability is recorded by a guarded module import. Calling `triton_moe_w1w3_silu` when Triton is unavailable raises a descriptive `ImportError`, and requested dimensions above the 8192 `d_ff` or `d_model` hard caps raise `ValueError` before launch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://models/moe_triton.py#L147-L181",
