    {
      "id": "claim_1a97bc6a67884bf69eb7ea5f7b95fd77",
      "statement": "Focused MoE tests protect router shapes, index bounds, weight normalization, auxiliary-loss finiteness and gradients, shared-expert activity, dispatch correctness, and deterministic output; Triton tests separately cover the CPU reference, empty expert ranges, missing-Triton and hard-cap failures, plus GPU FP32/BF16 kernel parity.",
